    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45122" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sponso</span></b> , āre, v. a.
		sponsus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to betroth</i>, <i>affiance</i>, <i>espouse</i> (post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					23, 2, 38</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tert. Vel. Virg.
			11</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Paul. Nol. Carm. 18, 43</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">et sponsabo te mihi in sempiternum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Osee, 2, 19</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 20</span></i>.</div>
